## 4. Performance Complexity, Memory Layout & Architecture Analysis

### 4.1 Asymptotic Time & Space Complexity

| Operation | Time Complexity | Space Complexity | Synchronization Primitive |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Point Read ($T_{\text{read}}$)** | $\mathcal{O}(\log N + |\mathcal{V}_K|)$ | $\mathcal{O}(1)$ | `memory_order_acquire` loads |
| **Point Write (CAS)** | $\mathcal{O}(\log N + 1)$ | $\mathcal{O}(1)$ (amortized) | Tagged Pointer `CAS` + `clwb` |
| **Range Scan $[K_1, K_2]$** | $\mathcal{O}(\log N + M \cdot |\mathcal{V}|)$ | $\mathcal{O}(M)$ | Lock-free forward traversal |
| **Epoch Reclamation Pass** | $\mathcal{O}(|Limbo| + T_{\text{threads}})$ | $\mathcal{O}(1)$ | Amortized thread-local frees |

---

### 4.2 NUMA Interconnect & Invalidation Traffic Analysis

Under high-skew Zipfian writes ($\alpha = 0.99$), sharing mutable pointers across NUMA sockets induces catastrophic **Cross-Socket Invalidation Storms** across Intel UPI / AMD Infinity Fabric:

```
Socket 0 (Cores 0-31)              Interconnect (UPI / IF)            Socket 1 (Cores 32-63)
+------------------------+        ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~        +------------------------+
| Local L1/L2 Cache      |                                         | Local L1/L2 Cache      |
| [TupleVersion: 64B]    | <=== Invalidation Requests (RFO) =====> | [TupleVersion: 64B]    |
| (Line state: MODIFIED) |                                         | (Line state: INVALID)  |
+------------------------+                                         +------------------------+
            |                                                                  |
            v                                                                  v
+------------------------+                                         +------------------------+
| NUMA 0 Node Memory     |                                         | NUMA 1 Node Memory     |
| [WAL Ring Buffer 0]    |                                         | [WAL Ring Buffer 1]    |
+------------------------+                                         +------------------------+
```

1. **False-Sharing Elimination:**
   * Every `TupleVersion`, `ThreadControlBlock`, and `WalRingBuffer` partition is `alignas(64)` aligned.
   * Atomic counters (`tx_create`, `tx_expire`, `lock_status`) are packed within a single 64-byte cacheline, meaning one cacheline fetch delivers all metadata for visibility arbitration in a single L1 data-cache fill.

2. **Partitioned WAL Pipeline:**
   * Writers only append to the thread's local NUMA WAL ring buffer, eliminating inter-socket interconnect traffic during log writes.

