---

## 3. Memory Ordering Rationale

| Operation | Memory Order | Rationale & Architectural Guarantee |
|---|---|---|
| `page_table[pid].head.load()` (Read Path) | `std::memory_order_acquire` | Prevents CPU/compiler from reordering dependent dereferences of `VersionNode::data` before loading the pointer. On ARM/POWER, emits `dmb.ld` / load-acquire barrier to invalidate speculative out-of-order reads of the node contents. |
| `page_table[pid].head.CAS()` (Commit) | `std::memory_order_release` | Enforces that all writes to the new `VersionNode` and WAL persistence acknowledgment happen-before the pointer becomes visible to concurrent readers. Prevents stores from floating below the publication point. |
| `WalSlot::sequence` (MPSC Ring Buffer) | `acquire` / `release` | Establishes a synchronized-with relationship between the enqueueing transaction thread and the single consumer flusher thread, ensuring the 4KB payload is fully written before the slot is marked valid. |
| `durable_lsn_watermark_` (Flusher $\to$ Workers) | `std::memory_order_release` | Ensures the disk I/O CQE completions and kernel write buffers are committed before worker threads unblock from the futex wait loop. |
| `global_epoch.fetch_add()` (EBR) | `std::memory_order_acq_rel` | Guarantees bidirectional serialization: prior reads of retired objects in epoch $e_k$ finish before advancement, and no memory allocations in $e_{k+1}$ are reordered prior to the epoch change. |

---

## 4. Formal Invariant Proofs & Edge-Case Analysis

### 4.1 Freedom from Data Races & ABA Hazards

* **Invariant 1 (Publication Order):** A version node $V_{new}$ containing data $D$ initialized at physical address $P$ cannot be read in an uninitialized state.
  $$\text{Store}(D) \xrightarrow{po} \text{CAS}_{rel}(\text{head}, V_{old}, V_{new}) \xrightarrow{sw} \text{Load}_{acq}(\text{head}) \xrightarrow{po} \text{Read}(D)$$
  By C++20 standard memory model [intro.races], sequenced-before ($\xrightarrow{po}$) combined with release-acquire synchronization ($\xrightarrow{sw}$) establishes a strict happens-before relation: $\text{Store}(D) \to \text{Read}(D)$. Thus, no reader ever observes a torn or partially constructed `VersionNode`.

* **Invariant 2 (ABA Hazard Prevention via EBR):** A version node $V_x$ cannot be retired and reallocated while an active reader holds a pointer to $V_x$.
  * Let reader $R$ enter critical section at epoch $e_k$.
  * Node $V_x$ is unlinked at epoch $e_m \ge e_k$ and enqueued to `retired_heads[e_m \pmod 3]`.
  * Node $V_x$ can only be physically freed when `global_epoch` advances to at least $e_m + 2$.
  * `global_epoch` cannot reach $e_m + 2$ while $R$'s `local_epoch` remains $e_k \le e_m$, because `try_advance_epoch()` validates $\forall i: \text{local\_epoch}_i \ge \text{global\_epoch}$.
  * Hence, $V_x$ remains resident in memory for the entire lifetime of $R$'s read traversal.

### 4.2 Out-of-Order LSN Completion Safety

`io_uring` can process multiple submitted Direct-I/O SQEs asynchronously across multi-queue NVMe hardware. CQEs may complete in non-monotonic order ($CQE_{k+1}$ finishes before $CQE_k$).

* **Proof of Safety:** The watermark update satisfies:
  $$\text{Watermark}_{t} = \max\left(\text{Watermark}_{t-1}, \min_{i \in \text{in-flight}} (\text{LSN}_i) \right)$$
  Transaction $T_k$ waiting for durability on $\text{LSN}_k$ remains blocked in `wait_durable(LSN_k)` via `futex_wait` until:
  $$\text{durable\_lsn\_watermark\_} \ge \text{LSN}_k$$
  Because the watermark only advances upon the persistence barrier (`IORING_FSYNC_DATASYNC`), transactions cannot publish their version node until all dependent prior LSNs have physically reached non-volatile media.

### 4.3 Torn Write Detection & Direct-I/O Alignment

1. **Alignment:** All I/O buffers are mapped to 4096-byte boundaries with sizes formatted to integer multiples of the NVMe physical sector size (4KB), fulfilling `O_DIRECT` direct memory transfer requirements without intermediate kernel buffering.
2. **Crash Invariant (Checksum Verification):** Each WAL block is wrapped with a 32-byte header containing an SSE4.2-accelerated `CRC32C` polynomial calculated over the trailing data:
   $$\text{CRC}_{\text{valid}} \iff \text{calculate\_crc32c}(\text{payload}, 4064) = \text{header.crc32c}$$
   Upon recovery, any partial block write caused by mid-flight power loss violates the CRC invariant, allowing the recovery engine to identify the torn tail and truncate cleanly at the last valid LSN.

---

## 5. Complexity Analysis

| Subsystem / Operation | Time Complexity (Amortized) | Space Complexity |
|---|---|---|
| **MVCC Read Traversal** | $O(k)$ ($k =$ chain length $\approx O(1)$ with pruning) | $O(1)$ auxiliary |
| **OCC Validation & Commit** | $O(1)$ wait-free CAS | $O(1)$ |
| **Lock-Free WAL Enqueue** | $O(1)$ wait-free via ring buffer slot CAS | $O(N)$ buffer slots ($N = 65536$) |
| **io_uring Batch Flush** | $O(B)$ per batch ($B \le 512$ SQEs) | $O(B \times \text{PAGE\_SIZE})$ static buffer |
| **EBR Memory Reclamation** | $O(1)$ per unlinked node batch | $O(\text{Versions in flight})$ |

