## 1. Formal Memory-Model & Concurrency Invariants

### 1.1 Axiomatic Ordering Proofs across Subsystems

```
Writer Thread (Delta Prepend / Commit)       Reader Thread (Traversal / Snapshot Read)
======================================       =========================================
[1] Construct DeltaNode / Version Data       [4] EpochGuard enters epoch (relaxed/acquire)
[2] Atomic CAS MappingTable (release/acq_rel) ---> [5] Atomic Load MappingTable (acquire)
    ↳ Synchronizes-With ---------------------> [6] Traverse Delta Chain (dereference payload)
[3] WAL Append / LSN Advance (release) ------> [7] Atomic Load GlobalLSN / Epoch (acquire)
```

#### Mapping Table Pointer Updates (`std::memory_order_release` / `std::memory_order_acquire`)
* **Invariant:** Any node initialization (writing payload, key-value pairs, predecessor links) must happen before the node address becomes visible to concurrent readers.
* **Proof:** Let $W$ be the store to the payload of node $N$, and let $CAS_{rel}(M[P], old, N)$ be the atomic release CAS on mapping table index $P$. Let $L_{acq}(M[P])$ be the atomic load in a reader thread returning $N$.
  $$W \xrightarrow{\text{sequenced-before}} CAS_{rel} \xrightarrow{\text{synchronizes-with}} L_{acq} \xrightarrow{\text{sequenced-before}} R(N)$$
  By transitivity of happens-before ($\xrightarrow{hb}$), $W \xrightarrow{hb} R(N)$. Thus, all non-atomic writes to $N$ are visible to the reader without data races.

#### Epoch Tracker Registration & Advancement (`std::memory_order_seq_cst` vs `acquire`/`release`)
* **Invariant:** A thread reading epoch-protected pointers must not access retired memory after the global epoch advances past the grace period.
* **Proof:** Thread entering reads global epoch $E_g$ via `load(memory_order_seq_cst)` and stores to thread-local active epoch $E_{local}$ via `store(memory_order_seq_cst)`. The epoch reclaimer increments $E_g$ using `fetch_add(1, memory_order_seq_cst)` and loads all $E_{local}$ via `load(memory_order_seq_cst)`.
  Sequential consistency guarantees a total global order $S$ over all operations on $E_g$ and $\{E_{local}^i\}$. There is no execution interleaving where a thread observes an unlinked pointer while being omitted from the reclaimer's snapshot of active threads.

#### WAL Tail Allocation & Record Ready Flag (`std::memory_order_acq_rel` / `std::memory_order_release`)
* **Invariant:** Log payload bytes written to the circular buffer must be visible to the group-commit flusher before the flusher processes the slice.
* **Proof:** A thread reserves buffer space $[T_{old}, T_{old} + S)$ using `tail_.fetch_add(S, memory_order_relaxed)`. After copying its record payload, it sets `record_header.ready.store(1, memory_order_release)`. The flusher inspects `record_header.ready.load(memory_order_acquire)`.
  The acquire load establishes a happens-before edge ensuring the entire variable-length log payload is coherent in CPU cache hierarchies prior to `io_uring_prep_write_fixed`.

---

## 2. Complete C++20 Storage Engine Implementation

```
                                +-------------------------------------------------------+
                                |               Logical PageID Indirection              |
                                +-------------------------------------------------------+
                                        |                               |
                                        v                               v
                             [ MappingTable (P=0) ]          [ MappingTable (P=1) ]
                                        |                               |
                                  Atomic CAS                      Atomic CAS
                                        |                               |
                                        v                               v
                              +--------------------+          +--------------------+
                              |  InsertDeltaNode   |          |   SplitDeltaNode   |
                              +--------------------+          +--------------------+
                                        |                               |
                                        v                               v
                              +--------------------+          +--------------------+
                              |  DeleteDeltaNode   |          | Consolidated Page  |
                              +--------------------+          +--------------------+
                                        |
                                        v
                              +--------------------+
                              | Consolidated Base  |
                              +--------------------+
```

The unified implementation below contains the complete transactional Bw-Tree, Epoch-Based Reclamation, Snapshot Isolation MVCC, and asynchronous `io_uring` WAL pipeline.

