## 3. Complexity & Benchmarking Characterization

### 3.1 Asymptotic Time Complexity

| Operation | Amortized Time | Worst-Case Time | Notes / Latency Contributors |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Point Read (`get`)** | $\mathcal{O}(\log_B N + L_{max})$ | $\mathcal{O}(\log_B N + L_{max})$ | Wait-free traversal; bounded delta-chain depth $L_{max} \le 8$. |
| **Delta Insert (`put`)** | $\mathcal{O}(1)$ | $\mathcal{O}(1 + \text{Retries})$ | Lock-free single CAS on Mapping Table slot; wait-free atomic WAL log reservation. |
| **Consolidation** | $\mathcal{O}(M \log M)$ | $\mathcal{O}(M \log M)$ | $M$ is the number of keys in base node + delta chain ($M \le 128$). |
| **Page Split (SMO)** | $\mathcal{O}(M)$ | $\mathcal{O}(M)$ | Two single-CAS updates: child `SplitDeltaNode` followed by parent `IndexDeltaNode`. |
| **WAL Group Commit** | $\mathcal{O}(1)$ | $\mathcal{O}(\text{I/O Flush Latency})$ | Amortized across all concurrent transactions batched in the kernel submission queue. |

---

### 3.2 Memory Layout & Alignment Breakdown

```
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| BwTreeNode Base (64-byte Cacheline Aligned)                                     |
+----------------------+--------------------+--------------------+----------------+
| type (1 Byte)        | chain_length (4 B) | padding (3 Bytes)  | next (8 Bytes) |
+----------------------+--------------------+--------------------+----------------+
| vtable ptr (8 Bytes) | EpochNode (0 B)    | Remainder Reserved (40 Bytes)       |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| InsertDeltaNode                                                                 |
+----------------------+--------------------+--------------------+----------------+
| key (8 Bytes)        | val (8 Bytes)      | commit_ts (8 Bytes)| Padding (32 B) |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

- **Per-Node Footprint:** Every delta record is aligned to $64$ bytes (`alignas(std::hardware_destructive_interference_size)`), eliminating false sharing across concurrent cores writing to adjacent addresses.
- **Mapping Table Footprint:** $1\text{M slots} \times 64\text{ bytes} = 64\text{ MB}$, resident in physical RAM.
- **Overhead Amortization:** Compacting after $L_{max} = 8$ bounds memory magnification to $\le 1.125\times$ base page storage.

---

### 3.3 Proof of Livelock and Deadlock Freedom

1. **Deadlock Freedom:**
   The design is strictly latch-free. Threads execute zero mutex acquisitions, conditional variable waits, or unbounded spinlocks during index traversal and delta mutations. Thus, the system is deadlocked-free by construction.
2. **Livelock & Starvation Freedom:**
   - For an individual thread $T_1$ attempting a CAS on Mapping Table slot $M[p]$, a failure occurs *if and only if* another thread $T_2$ succeeded in committing a modification to $M[p]$.
   - Global progress is strictly monotonic:
     $$\sum_{\forall p} \text{Successful\_CAS}(M[p])(t + \Delta t) > \sum_{\forall p} \text{Successful\_CAS}(M[p])(t)$$
   - The ring buffer WAL reservation uses atomic `fetch_add`, which is strictly wait-free ($\mathcal{O}(1)$ step bound).

