## 4. Complexity, Memory Overhead & Progress Guarantees

### 4.1 Time Complexity Analysis

| Operation | Best Case | Amortized | Worst Case ($L = L_{max}$) | Justification |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Read (Snapshot)** | $\mathcal{O}(\log_B N)$ | $\mathcal{O}(\log_B N + L)$ | $\mathcal{O}(\log_B N + L_{max})$ | Bw-Tree search traverses tree height $\log_B N$ followed by chain of length at most $L_{max} = 8$. |
| **Insert / Update** | $\mathcal{O}(\log_B N)$ | $\mathcal{O}(\log_B N + \frac{\text{Cost}(Consolidate)}{L_{max}})$ | $\mathcal{O}(\log_B N + K \log K)$ | Lock-free single CAS prepend to mapping table. Amortized consolidation triggered once every $L_{max}$ operations. |
| **Consolidation** | $\mathcal{O}(K)$ | $\mathcal{O}(K \log K)$ | $\mathcal{O}(K \log K)$ | Gathering $K$ records across delta chain and sorting/deduplicating MVCC versions. |
| **WAL Group-Commit** | $\mathcal{O}(1)$ | $\mathcal{O}(1)$ | $\mathcal{O}(\text{FlushLatency})$ | Tail reservation is wait-free fetch-add; physical submission is batched across concurrent threads via `io_uring`. |

### 4.2 Per-Node Memory Overhead Breakdown

| Structure Component | Size (Bytes) | Alignment | Purpose & Optimization |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `MappingTable` Slot | 8 | 64 | Cacheline-aligned atomic `TaggedPointer` (48-bit ptr, 16-bit sequence/chain length). |
| `InsertDeltaNode` | 40 | 8 | `NodeHeader` (16B) + `next` pointer (8B) + `Record` payload (24B) + packing optimizations. |
| `SplitDeltaNode` | 32 | 8 | `NodeHeader` (16B) + `next` pointer (8B) + `split_key` (8B) + `sibling_page_id` (8B). |
| `BaseLeafPage` | 48 + $K \times 24$ | 64 | Vector header + bounds + contiguous cache-friendly sorted records array. |
| `ThreadControlBlock`| 64 | 64 | `alignas(hardware_destructive_interference_size)` to eliminate CPU cacheline bouncing during epoch reads. |

### 4.3 Progress Guarantees

```
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Operation Path               | Progress Guarantee | Invariant / Mechanism                   |
+------------------------------+--------------------+-----------------------------------------+
| WAL Reservation              | Wait-Free          | Atomic fetch_add (Bounded O(1) steps)   |
| Read (Traversal)             | Lock-Free          | Traverses immutable delta pointers      |
| Insert (Prepend)             | Lock-Free          | Single CAS retry loop on mapping table  |
| Page Consolidation           | Lock-Free          | Single CAS; aborts safely on race       |
| Epoch Check-In / Check-Out   | Wait-Free          | Unconditional atomic stores             |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

1. **Deadlock Freedom:** The engine contains zero mutexes, condition variables, or blocking spinlocks in its read, write, and index paths. Circular waiting conditions cannot form ($\mathcal{G}_{\text{wait}} = \emptyset$).
2. **Livelock Prevention:** Contention on the mapping table is resolved via Compare-And-Swap. Under simultaneous updates to the same logical page, at least one thread succeeds in each CAS step, guaranteeing **system-wide lock-free progress**.
3. **Consolidation Convergence:** Failed consolidation CAS attempts result in immediate deallocation via the `EpochManager` without retrying on the modified chain, preventing duplicate consolidation runs from degrading throughput.
